 # Route task update --interactive through the consistency guards
 
@@ -15,4 +15,12 @@
 
 It was trivial. task-update.ts's --interactive branch wrote via writeTaskFileAuditably directly, bypassing all 4 consistency guards and the COMPLETE-requires-resolution check. Fix: parse both pre-edit and post-edit content, diff just the 4 guard-relevant fields (new diffGuardRelevantFields() in task-cmd-helpers.ts, comparing parsed Task state rather than requiring a structured diff up front -- an interactive edit can touch anything), and feed that diff into the existing enforceUpdateFieldGuards orchestrator, same as every other path. No new guard logic. The COMPLETE-requires-resolution check is applied separately against the edited task's resulting state directly, since its same-call semantics don't map cleanly onto a free-text diff.
 
 Verified: 11 new unit tests for diffGuardRelevantFields (task-cmd-helpers.test.ts), plus an end-to-end CLI smoke test with a scripted $EDITOR against a real invocation (bun run packages/trail/src/index.ts) confirming: violation blocked with file left unmodified, --force warns and proceeds, a fixed violation succeeds silently on retry, and an edit touching neither guarded field passes through untouched. 426/427 tests pass (1 known pre-existing jj/git storage-cmd flake, confirmed clears on retry). tsc/biome clean.
